1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,850
Meet TontinePilot, the AI copilot for community savings groups. The dashboard shows this cycle's collection, who paid, and who still owes.

2
00:00:10,271 --> 00:00:21,771
Declare a payment in plain English. Just type: I paid twenty thousand for Awa. The AI extracts the amount and the recipient — and refuses to guess when it cannot read.

3
00:00:21,871 --> 00:00:30,221
Run several savings groups side by side. Switch in one click, archive the paused ones, or create a new group in two minutes.

4
00:00:30,571 --> 00:00:38,946
Creating a group takes two minutes: name, amount in francs or dollars, members with history, AI rotation preview, done.

5
00:00:39,409 --> 00:00:48,409
Every member gets a trust score that heals when they pay. Reliable payers collect early. New members join mid-group with automatic catch-up.

6
00:00:48,897 --> 00:00:56,772
Late payments trigger kind, automatic reminders. And the audio digest reads the whole cycle summary out loud.

7
00:00:56,872 --> 00:01:04,097
The emergency fund is a real menu now: top it up, cover critical lates from it, track every repayment.

8
00:01:04,451 --> 00:01:10,326
Export the full ledger to a spreadsheet in one click. No more arguments about who paid what.

9
00:01:10,426 --> 00:01:16,426
And Tonti, the built-in assistant, answers live questions and nudges late members for you.

10
00:01:16,526 --> 00:01:20,701
TontinePilot. Community savings, minus the drama.
